The aging of the population has increased the demand for systems capable of assisting in the monitoring of people who require continuous care.
In this context, we present the development of a system based on Deep Learning models for sentiment analysis using images and videos, focusing on pain detection.
The system was developed in Python, using the OpenCV library for frame capture and the vision models for Visual Question Answering and Image-Text Matching tasks.
Initially, the presence of people in the images is identified,and then the sentiment classification is determined between the classes "with pain" and "without pain".
For performance evaluation, a database composed of 199 images was used (https://github.com/fabiorcerqueira/pain_nopain_img_rep).
This images were validated through Google Forms (https://github.com/fabiorcerqueira/create_form_for_img_human_validation/tree/main).
The proposed framework/system may assist professionals and caregivers in the early identification of risk situations involving people with special needs.
